# Trivy ignore file.
#
# POLICY: this file starts EMPTY and must stay that way unless a finding is
# demonstrably a false positive for this application, or is unreachable from
# any code path this service executes.
#
# Every entry MUST record, in the comment directly above it:
#   - WHY the vulnerability does not apply here (not "we'll fix it later")
#   - the date it was added and who reviewed it
#   - an expiry date, so the entry is revisited rather than inherited forever
#
# Ignoring a real vulnerability to make the pipeline green defeats the purpose
# of the security gate. If a High/Critical CVE is genuine, upgrade the
# dependency instead.
#
# Format (one CVE id per line, optional expiry):
#
#   # CVE-0000-00000 affects the XML parsing path of some-lib. This application
#   # only uses its JSON codec, which is unaffected. Reviewed 2026-08-28.
#   CVE-0000-00000 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Scope: this file is honoured by every Trivy stage in the pipeline —
# dependency_scan (application JAR), trivy_fs (repository) and trivy_image
# (container). An entry added here silences the finding everywhere, so scope
# each justification accordingly.
